    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and table-setting, led by **Sam Antonacci**, who paces the lineup with an efficiency score of 63.61. Batting out of the leadoff spot against the mid-tier xERA of 4.36 posted by Kumar Rocker, **Sam Antonacci** benefits from a massive 10% boost for his high-leverage order position and a favorable platoon matchup that reinforces his status as our primary engine for runs and stolen bases. Close behind is **Nasim Nunez**, whose 61.73 score is driven by a highly favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner. While **Nasim Nunez** is traditionally slotted lower in the order, his ability to exploit a 5.10 xERA\u2014the highest on the board today\u2014makes him a high-floor play, particularly given the aggressive baserunning mandates for the Waves.\n\nWhile the core is set, **Jackson Merrill** presents the most nuanced start of the day. Despite a challenging matchup against the 3.28 xERA of Braxton Ashcraft, **Jackson Merrill** maintains a 51.66 efficiency score, buoyed by a 13% boost from his platoon advantage. We are banking on his ability to neutralize top-tier pitching through volume, though we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for him and **Liam Hicks** (47.27) to ensure no late-scratch risks materialize. **Liam Hicks** is hovering near the \"Marginal\" threshold; should he drop out of the #4 spot in the official lineup, we will be forced to reconsider his viability to preserve our limited game caps. \n\nThe decision-making process was hampered by the absence of heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, all of whom are sidelined due to team off-days. Consequently, **Miguel Vargas** (55.00) was locked into the 1B slot by default, serving as our most reliable depth piece for today's specific rotation. With the roster currently light on star-power due to the schedule, the onus is on the speed-oriented trio of **Sam Antonacci**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Jackson Merrill** to manufacture runs. We will keep a close eye on weather developments, but as it stands, no significant atmospheric warnings are flagged for today\u2019s games. Our bench, featuring secondary options like **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg**, remains on high alert should any late lineup changes affect our projected scoring floor.",
